    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="11" relname="background">This is a good start on flexibility and efficiency.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="11" relname="span">Just for more ways to consider flexibility, it could very well be that a system is flexible</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="elaboration">(provides different ways to perform the same function),</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="10" relname="span">but that MIGHT effect learnability.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="13" relname="span">With more than one way to perform a function, one has to learn and retain in memory how to do the same thing in different ways.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="elaboration">There is where the efficiency aspect comes through.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="8" relname="circumstance">When the process is logical and intuitive, and learned once,</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="14" relname="span">then there is a good chance that flexibility will be a positive thing.</segment>
        <group id="9" type="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="15" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="multinuc" parent="4" relname="evidence"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="contrast"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="12" relname="contrast"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="10" relname="concession"/>
    </body>
</rst>
